  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 200 AM CDT Tue Oct 6 2026\n\nWednesday-Early Next Week:\nFurther warming occurs into mid-week as 850mb temperatures\napproach 16 to 18 C. This will correlate to high temperatures in\nthe middle to upper 80s. This is 10+ degrees above normal for\nearly October. Despite the abnormally warm temperatures, it\nappears we will remain shy of any record highs in the lower 90s.\nOverall, confidence is high in the anomalous warm weather\nthrough this week and weekend, as gleaned by the small NBM\ninterquartile spreads.\n\nAdditionally, the dry pattern is expected to persist with\nminimal PoPs in the forecast. The next \"chance\" for any\nmeasurable precipitation occurs with passing energy to the east\nof the area from tropical remnants lifting out of the Gulf. \nConfidence is low in this potential, with PoPs of 10 to 15 \npercent glancing southeast MO late Sunday. Ensemble guidance \ncontinues to favor a mostly dry scenario for the area. \nOtherwise, guidance hint at some low confidence PoPs early next\nweek as an upper level trough translates into the northern US. \nWith that being said, the storyline remains the same with dry \nweather and worsening drought conditions. Daily minimum relative\nhumidity values around 20 to 35 percent remain likely, with \nlight winds limiting fire weather concerns for the time being.\nWorsening drought conditions may further amplify the Fall fire \ndanger as we progress through October.",
